From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:09:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 157/191] [ae-patch] Show the insertion line when a sidebar row
 moves to another project, Sessions or Triage group

A drop on a row of another list now files the dragged row there (another
project folder, or Sessions to unfile it) or, under Triage, sets the status
of the group it lands in, then places it on the side the insertion line
showed, saved in the manual order like a same-list drag. A row landing in
another list is always ranked, even where the order looks unchanged, or it
would show there by recency. The line follows the pointer's half of the row
under it. Shared rows and the other groupings keep upstream's drops. A
refused status write leaves the row where it was. The server's PATCH now
deletes an empty ae.status (No status) instead of storing it.
